.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead ready" 1  "bead ready " 
.SH NAME
bead ready \- Show only ready frontier issues
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead ready\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-jsonl\fR] [\fB\-\-assignee\fR] [\fB\-\-sort\fR] [\fB\-\-comments\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-all\fR] [\fB\-\-count\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Shortcut for `bead list \-\-ready`: every flag behaves exactly as it
does on `list`, with \-\-ready forced on.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead ready                        # Same as: bead list \-\-ready
  bead ready \-\-json                 # Same as: bead list \-\-ready \-\-json
  bead ready \-\-sort attempts \-\-json # Same as: bead list \-\-ready \-\-sort attempts \-\-json
  bead ready \-\-count                # How many issues are ready right now
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output one JSON array
.TP
\fB\-\-jsonl\fR
Output one JSON object per line (empty results write no bytes)
.TP
\fB\-\-assignee\fR \fI<ASSIGNEE>\fR
Filter by assignee
.TP
\fB\-\-sort\fR \fI<ORDER>\fR
Ready\-frontier ordering: attempts prefers fewer consecutive failures within each priority tier, then retains the FIFO tie\-breakers
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
attempts
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-comments\fR \fI<COMMENTS>\fR [default: none]
Comment projection: none, unresolved, or all (default: none)
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<FIELDS>\fR
Comma\-separated projection of cli_issue document members (FIELD PROJECTION); without it every member is emitted
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: auto]
Notes projection: auto, none, tail:N, or all (default: auto)
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 100]
Maximum number of issues to return (0\-999999)
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Ignore \-\-limit and return every ready issue
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR
Print only the number of ready issues (ignores \-\-limit/\-\-all)
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show diagnostic information about filtering (SQL query, counts, exclusion reasons)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
